# Windows never runs `make stow` — nothing here is a dotfile. The package exists
# so the Windows side of a multi-boot machine is tracked next to the others, and
# this file exists so `make stow-test`, which stows every package, leaves the
# throwaway $HOME empty.
#
# Stow ignores `^/README.*` by default, but a local ignore file replaces the
# whole default list rather than extending it, so the usual entries are repeated.
^/README.*
^/apply\.ps1$
^/apps\.txt$
^/bootstrap\.ps1$
^/registry$
^/\.stow-local-ignore$
\.git
\.gitignore
.+~
\#.*\#
